
export anchor Story_126d4b89c161d7b7:
    userPrompt:
        \\\
        The Planning board has a new "Draft" column, the first on the board,
        to the left of the Backlog. It holds rough stories: ideas written down
        quickly that aren't ready to plan yet. The spec has nothing on a Draft
        column yet, so this is new. Update every place that lists the columns
        or decides which ones can hold stories:

        - spec/scope/planning/index.pi#Planning.description and
          spec/scope/planning/index.pi#Planning.layout give the column order as
          Draft, Backlog, Next sprint, Current sprint, Done, Findings. Draft
          gets a status icon and top-edge colour of its own, as
          spec/scope/planning/index.pi#Planning.parts gives every column: for
          example, a pencil in the theme's tertiary text colour. Its look must
          be clearly different from the Backlog's dashed circle.
        - Stories are written in Draft the same way as in the Backlog and Next
          sprint, as spec/scope/planning/index.pi#Planning.creating says: an
          "Add story" line, "+ Add" on hover, and Ctrl+N when Draft has focus.
        - Draft takes drops, as spec/scope/planning/index.pi#Planning.sprint
          describes for the Backlog and Next sprint. Stories move between Draft
          and the Backlog by dragging, with Alt+Left/Alt+Right
          (spec/scope/planning/index.pi#Planning.keyboard), and from a card's
          menu ("Move to draft"; "Move to backlog" from Draft). Draft stories
          can be selected, and the bulk bar can move them
          (spec/scope/planning/index.pi#Planning.parts). A Draft story never
          reaches a sprint without first moving to the Backlog or Next sprint.
        - Draft's empty state, worded as in
          spec/scope/planning/index.pi#Planning.states, says something like
          "No drafts. Jot an idea down here."
        - The Draft section is saved in order.json with the others, as
          spec/scope/planning/index.pi#Planning.saving and
          spec/scope/project-data/index.pi#ProjectData.contents say. A plan
          saved before Draft existed loads with Draft empty.

        Accepted proposals still go into the Backlog, as they do today. The
        column is named "Draft"; keep it clearly apart from the existing
        "Draft stories" button on the Backlog's heading.
        \\\

    mode: combined

    model: opus
